      en: "Hawassa Industrial Park (HIP) is the flagship project of Ethiopia's ambitious industrialization strategy and stands as one of the largest and most advanced industrial zones in Africa. Officially inaugurated in 2016, the park specifically focuses on the textile and garment industry, aiming to boost export earnings and create large-scale employment. Located in Hawassa, the capital of the Sidama Region, HIP was designed as an 'eco-industrial park,' featuring a state-of-the-art Zero Liquid Discharge (ZLD) water treatment facility to safeguard the local ecosystem. The park hosts over 50 international and local garment manufacturers, providing jobs for tens of thousands of workers, predominantly young women. Its integrated infrastructure includes on-site customs, banking, and government services to streamline business operations. Strategically positioned along the major highway to Addis Ababa, HIP serves as a primary model for Ethiopia's network of industrial parks. It remains a central pillar of the nation's goal to become a leading manufacturing hub in sub-Saharan Africa.",
